  "construction": {
   "name": "complete_rectangular_prism_column_return",
   "proof": "COMPLETE RECTANGULAR COLUMN RETURN\n15 October 2026\n\nThe preceding octagonal face-contact return produced 63 complete owners\nin nine square-footprint columns, with seven owners per column. Preserve\nthat unequal-phase return separately. The following regular-phase product\nis a second complete geometry with the same ideal enclosure, and transfers\nthe physical mechanism to every prism height.\n\nLet R be the fixed proper frame that aligns an actual prism side-face\nnormal with the x axis. For regular 8- and 12-prisms this is the specified\nrotation pi/k from their canonical vertex-to-x frame. For the other prism\nfamilies retain the canonical frame. No frame is selected by a metric\nsearch. Let l_j <= (Rv)_j <= u_j be rigorous bounds for every vertex v of\nthe complete canonical prism. Put m_j=(u_j+l_j)/2 and choose the rational\ncell width W_j strictly greater than u_j-l_j. Convexity places the whole\nowner R P - m strictly inside its axis-parallel cell of widths W_j.\n\nFor positive integers A,B,C, put complete owners at\n  c(i,j,k)=((i-(A-1)/2)W_x,(j-(B-1)/2)W_y,(k-(C-1)/2)W_z)-m\nfor 0<=i<A, 0<=j<B, 0<=k<C. Distinct index triples differ in a coordinate,\nso the corresponding open cell interiors are disjoint and their complete\nowners are strictly separated in that coordinate. Every owner lies in the\nbox A W_x by B W_y by C W_z, hence in a cube of side\n  S=max(A W_x,B W_y,C W_z).\nThe enclosing cube has the common center 0. Deleting any explicit subset\nof whole owners preserves both properties and retains all boundary costs.\n\nFor ideal prism widths w_x,w_y,w_z the same construction has nominal\ncapacity floor(S/w_x)floor(S/w_y)floor(S/w_z). Its only changes occur at\nthe explicit events S=m w_j. Taking the first event with capacity>=N is\nan exact finite consequence of the product construction, not a packing\noptimality claim. The witness generator uses outward rational W_j and\nchecks the complete native geometry afterward.\n\nThis is a classical rectangular product packing. PingYou Ltd supplies\nthe new finite assemblies and complete certificates that improve the\npinned current prism records; no invention of Cartesian-product packing,\nof the regular polygon, or of the infinite contact lattices is claimed.\nThese assemblies use no published finite donor packing. Current record\nauthors remain in the separately retained baseline witnesses.\n\nThe unequal-phase octagonal source return and this equal-phase grid must\nnot be identified as the same marked continuation state. Both survive in\nthe record tree. No density or global optimality statement follows here.\n",
